WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.913
Why does the mode matter so much?

2
00:00:01.913 --> 00:00:04.286
Because, as Microsoft Learn puts it,

3
00:00:04.286 --> 00:00:08.213
detection mode only logs, and
only prevention mode blocks.

4
00:00:08.213 --> 00:00:13.300
By the end of this chapter you can check
every WAF policy against Microsoft's Zero

5
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:18.843
Trust recommendations, find every internet-facing
application gateway and Front Door

6
00:00:18.843 --> 00:00:23.475
profile that has no WAF or no logs,
compute the guide's prevention coverage,

7
00:00:23.475 --> 00:00:27.271
and hand the application owner
the exact command that moves

8
00:00:27.271 --> 00:00:30.688
a policy to prevention, without
the kit ever sending it.

9
00:00:30.688 --> 00:00:34.120
It's for application owners
who tune and switch the WAF,

10
00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:39.050
platform owners who own the policies,
and security monitors who read the logs.
